             The mode to convert the image to. If `None`, the native mode of the image is used.
+        crop_margin (`int`, *optional*):
+            Number of pixels to crop from each of the four edges of the image when decoding, for example to
+            remove a watermark or a border. If `None` or `0`, the image is not cropped. A margin that would
+            leave nothing of the image (twice the margin is not smaller than the width and the height) is
+            ignored and the image is returned uncropped.
         decode (`bool`, defaults to `True`):
             Whether to decode the image data. If `False`,
